## Server Configuration

The startup script (`start_vllm.sh`) uses these defaults:

| Parameter | Value | Description |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| `--model` | /data/lch/Models/Modelscope/Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct | Model path |
| `--served-model-name` | Qwen/Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct | API model name |
| `--tensor-parallel-size` | 1 | Number of GPUs for tensor parallelism |
| `--quantization` | fp8 | 8-bit floating point quantization |
| `--gpu-memory-utilization` | 0.9 | GPU memory usage ratio |
| `--max-model-len` | 8192 | Maximum sequence length |
| `--enforce-eager` | true | Disable CUDA graph for compatibility |
| `--dtype` | auto | Automatic dtype selection |
| `--port` | 1285 | Server port |

## Environment

- **Conda Environment**: `vllm_lch`
- **vLLM Version**: 0.16.0
- **GPU**: CUDA device 1

## Troubleshooting

### Check if server is running
```bash
curl http://localhost:1285/v1/models
```

### Check GPU usage
```bash
nvidia-smi
```

### Stop server
```bash
pkill -f "Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct"
```

### Out of Memory
Reduce `--gpu-memory-utilization` or `--max-model-len`:
```bash
bash start_vllm.sh --gpu-memory-utilization 0.8 --max-model-len 4096
```

### Slow Performance
Disable `--enforce-eager` for CUDA graph optimization (if memory allows):
```bash
# Edit start_vllm.sh to remove --enforce-eager
```
